WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.118
When the Lok Sabha is dissolved,

2
00:00:02.118 --> 00:00:03.578
do all pending bills die?

3
00:00:03.778 --> 00:00:04.887
Not all of them.

4
00:00:05.337 --> 00:00:07.385
Article 107 sets the rule.

5
00:00:07.535 --> 00:00:08.995
A bill pending in the Lok

6
00:00:08.995 --> 00:00:09.754
Sabha lapses.

7
00:00:09.874 --> 00:00:11.377
So does one the Lok Sabha

8
00:00:11.377 --> 00:00:12.880
passed that is pending in

9
00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:13.842
the Rajya Sabha.

10
00:00:14.292 --> 00:00:15.815
But a bill pending in the

11
00:00:15.815 --> 00:00:17.459
Rajya Sabha, not yet passed

12
00:00:17.459 --> 00:00:18.495
by the Lok Sabha,

13
00:00:18.595 --> 00:00:19.619
survives.

14
00:00:20.069 --> 00:00:21.913
Article 108 adds one more

15
00:00:21.913 --> 00:00:22.650
exception.

16
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:24.070
If the President notified

17
00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:25.390
a joint sitting before the

18
00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:26.000
dissolution,

19
00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:27.376
that sitting can still be

20
00:00:27.376 --> 00:00:28.703
held, and the bill passed.

21
00:00:29.153 --> 00:00:30.779
And prorogation, which only

22
00:00:30.779 --> 00:00:32.224
ends a session, makes no

23
00:00:32.224 --> 00:00:32.886
bill lapse.

24
00:00:33.336 --> 00:00:34.731
So ask where the bill is

25
00:00:34.731 --> 00:00:36.301
sitting, not how old it is.

26
00:00:36.801 --> 00:00:37.676
Your turn.

27
00:00:37.826 --> 00:00:39.155
Which bill does not lapse

28
00:00:39.155 --> 00:00:40.855
when the Lok Sabha is dissolved?
